{
  "$comment": [
    "The draft-07 verdicts pm.response.to.have.jsonSchema (the engine's native validator, core/schema_validation.hpp) and the shelf's ajv 6.12.5 and tv4 1.3.0 must agree on (#2656); script_json_schema_conformance_test.cpp runs every datum through all of them.",
    "`valid` is the verdict each validator gives. `tv4: false` marks a case outside tv4's draft-04 reach (a draft-06/07 keyword, which tv4 ignores, or a format, which tv4 checks only when one is added) or one tv4 answers against the specification (a length in UTF-16 code units rather than characters); the other validators still run it.",
    "`ignoredByAjv` lists the keywords the native validator does not evaluate and so refuses to pass on (collect_unevaluated_keywords): ajv 6 ignores each of them by default, so its verdict leaves the keyword out and it answers valid for each row's datum. None is a keyword ajv evaluates.",
    "`divergences` are the data the validators answer differently, each with both verdicts and why. They are kept out of `cases` and asserted as they stand, so a change on either side fails until its row moves into `cases`.",
    "Every verdict was checked against the unbundled ajv 6.12.5 and tv4 1.3.0 on Node."
  ],
